  "description": "UJAWAF crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P -4 21 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C148 H112 Gd8 N12 O44 Si1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1F (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2F (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1G (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2G (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.805-4.508 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.93-126.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd8L8(C6H4NH2COO)4SiO4] (C148H112Gd8N12O44Si).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
